 "new_string": "## Supported rule and caution\nThe task links a long color-2 line with an irregular pattern, with a full color-8 line parallel to the 2-line, aligned on the far side of the pattern. In demos the pattern is translated toward this new 8 boundary while preserving pattern colors. In the validated test, the diagonal 5 pair next to the 2 line predicts a full vertical 8 line three columns to the left; original 5s and 2 stripe stay unchanged. Do not assume future instances have identical orientation, spacing, or pattern movement without replaying current demos. Validate dimensions and every changed cell.\n\n## Additional validated horizontal instance (9x27)\nInput: background 1; full-width color-2 stripe at row 4; horizontal color-3 segment at row 1, columns 16–20. Correct output retained the stripe and segment in place, added a full-width color-8 line at row 2 (one row below the segment, immediately toward the stripe), and removed the original segment from row 1. In this arrangement the stripe is two rows below the marker segment, and the marker moves one step toward it while the 8 boundary is placed one step behind it. Unlike the earlier long-pattern examples, a single segment need not move an additional step to become adjacent to the stripe; use the one-cell translation toward color-2. This was accepted on first submission."
